00:59:09.060 --> 00:59:13.830
So you go to do the
electron specific heat,

00:59:13.830 --> 00:59:17.220
you will find out
electron specific heat

00:59:17.220 --> 00:59:24.420
approximately metal is
1/2 pi squared N over v.

00:59:24.420 --> 00:59:26.670
N is number of electrons.

00:59:26.670 --> 00:59:32.674
And kBT over TF.

00:59:32.674 --> 00:59:38.550
TF is the Fermi temperature.

00:59:38.550 --> 00:59:42.590
So electron temperature,
specific heat,

00:59:42.590 --> 00:59:45.470
is a temperature--

00:59:45.470 --> 00:59:49.760
is a function linearly
proportional to temperature.

00:59:49.760 --> 00:59:59.275
And so what's the TF is kBTF
equals Ef, Fermi energy.

01:00:02.810 --> 01:00:07.820
