01:16:29.990 --> 01:16:33.652
you put, let's say, E minus Ef.

01:16:33.652 --> 01:16:37.670
So 0 is the Ef here.

01:16:37.670 --> 01:16:40.010
And you put the atom in--

01:16:40.010 --> 01:16:42.230
say you put in some
impurity atoms,

01:16:42.230 --> 01:16:45.950
and they could create
some sharp features

01:16:45.950 --> 01:16:47.870
in the density of states.

01:16:47.870 --> 01:16:49.400
And those sharp
features could be

01:16:49.400 --> 01:16:52.202
very interesting for
transport because if you

01:16:52.202 --> 01:16:53.660
have sharp features,
it means there

01:16:53.660 --> 01:16:56.900
could be a lot of charge there.

01:16:56.900 --> 01:17:03.815
And the velocity of this
carrier is the slope.

01:17:06.490 --> 01:17:12.720
If I have-- so it's the slope--

01:17:12.720 --> 01:17:15.580
[? group ?] velocity is
the slope of this line.

01:17:15.580 --> 01:17:16.700
It's the dispersion lines.

01:17:20.100 --> 01:17:23.970
So typically, and for example
when we do thermoelectrics,

01:17:23.970 --> 01:17:28.980
we like those who have those
sharp features because I like

01:17:28.980 --> 01:17:33.480
to have a lot of charge
so that I can have

01:17:33.480 --> 01:17:34.890
high electric conductivity.

01:17:34.890 --> 01:17:37.200
It's the density
of states times--

01:17:37.200 --> 01:17:41.040
the [? number ?] density
is, say, F times D.

01:17:41.040 --> 01:17:44.700
And if the D is large,
I could potentially

01:17:44.700 --> 01:17:47.640
get a very high
[? number ?] density.

01:17:47.640 --> 01:17:49.495
And then, of course,
I have to care

01:17:49.495 --> 01:17:50.620
about the other properties.

01:17:50.620 --> 01:17:53.310
So I have to align
my Fermi level.

01:17:53.310 --> 01:17:57.610
And how I align my Fermi level
is by controlling the doping.

01:17:57.610 --> 01:18:02.800
So I can change the doping
and change that formula.

01:18:02.800 --> 01:18:07.390
So I thought I'll stop here.

01:18:07.390 --> 01:18:09.880
Any questions?

01:18:09.880 --> 01:18:11.340
I was looking at the papers.

01:18:11.340 --> 01:18:12.960
And I could go to--

01:18:12.960 --> 01:18:16.230
if you go to Physics
Today website,

01:18:16.230 --> 01:18:19.290
for example, you'll see
people doing cold atoms.

01:18:19.290 --> 01:18:21.630
What the cold atoms
mean, you know

01:18:21.630 --> 01:18:25.010
it will be relatable to
Bose-Einstein composition.

01:18:25.010 --> 01:18:29.020
A lot of flux on cold atoms.

01:18:29.020 --> 01:18:30.570
OK?

